ClassReserve
Static HTML/CSS/JavaScript frontend using Supabase Auth and Postgres.
Files
`index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`: website
`supabase-config.js`: browser-safe Supabase Project URL and Publishable key only
`SETUP-SUPABASE.sql`: database migration for reservation ownership, role-based access, and automatic status history
Required setup
In `supabase-config.js`, set `CLASSRESERVE_SUPABASE_URL` to the Supabase Project URL (for example `https://PROJECT_REF.supabase.co`, without `/rest/v1/`).
Set `CLASSRESERVE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` to the `sb_publishable_...` key. Never put an `sb_secret_...` or service-role key in browser code.
In Supabase SQL Editor, inspect existing `profiles` and `reservations` columns, then run `SETUP-SUPABASE.sql`. This expects `profiles.id` to match the Auth user UUID and `profiles.role` values `Student`, `Faculty`, or `Admin`.
In Supabase Authentication → URL Configuration, set the Site URL to your deployed website URL and add that same URL to Redirect URLs. Password reset emails require this configuration and an enabled email provider.
Commit the updated files to GitHub; Vercel should redeploy automatically.
Account setup
Each user must exist in Supabase Authentication and have a matching `public.profiles` row with the same UUID. The frontend does not create accounts or assign roles. Only an administrator should create or change Admin profiles.
Features
Supabase email/password login
Forgot-password email and password update flow
Student/Faculty room requests and personal request status
Admin request queue with Approve/Reject actions
Database trigger automatically records each new request and every status change in `reservation_history`
Color-coded navigation and request statuses
Important
Before running the SQL migration on a live database, make a backup and confirm the existing schema. If existing reservation rows do not have `user_id` populated, those old rows will not appear in users' personal lists. Test with non-sensitive sample requests first.
